From 254b49373fda034c8df5d6378befe592bcfc55f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Govindarajulu Varadarajan <govindarajulu.varadarajan@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Oct 2025 20:11:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 143/190] xilinx-ai-engine: free user_event1 irq in
 aie_part_release

commit 498d59ef0d4c2c145f66caa21ba3236753a0dfa3 from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

Explicitly free user_event1 irq thread in aie_part_release. Without
this, interrupt could occur during put_device() and free of devm
resources. Order of free is unknown and could lead to use after free
and undefined behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Govindarajulu Varadarajan <govindarajulu.varadarajan@amd.com>
Acked-by: Gregory Williams <gregory.williams@amd.com>
Message-ID: <20251003031202.2319372-4-govindarajulu.varadarajan@amd.com>
State: pending
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-part.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-part.c b/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-part.c
index 30b3e82b7dad..979d277d6908 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-part.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-part.c
@@ -680,6 +680,12 @@ static int aie_part_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *filp)
 	aie_part_rscmgr_reset(apart);
 
 	mutex_unlock(&apart->mlock);
+	if (apart->adev->dev_gen == AIE_DEVICE_GEN_AIE2PS) {
+		struct aie_aperture *aperture = apart->aperture;
+		int npi_irq = (apart->partition_id % AIE_USER_EVENT1_NUM_IRQ) + 1;
+
+		devm_free_irq(&apart->dev, aperture->npi_irq[npi_irq], apart);
+	}
 	aie_part_remove(apart);
 
 	return 0;
-- 
